known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks.\" (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T65 — `MetricsCollector`, `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricScope`, `MetricSource`.\n  - T66 — `golden_anchors.json` and the JSON benchmark report from `cognitive_workspace_benchmark`.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/` — current daemon binary location; the new CLI binary lives alongside.\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` (from T04) — provides the baseline column for the report.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/` — the canonical metrics module.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Observability`, `## Tests as documentation`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 9 and §Measurable Success Criteria in full.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report.rs` exposing: (a) `ReportInput { current: Vec<MetricValue>, baseline: Option<Vec<MetricValue>>, benchmark_report_path: PathBuf, scope: MetricScope, success_criteria: SuccessCriteriaThresholds }`; (b) `RegressionReport` rendering per-signal current value, baseline value, delta, target threshold (from spec §Measurable Success Criteria), pass/fail per row; (c) renderers for human-readable text, machine-readable JSON, and a CI-friendly summary line; (d) per-signal evidence pointer back to the contributing event/memory IDs so any regression is investigable. `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` encodes the spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets explicitly (30%, 40%, 80%, 0, 0, 90%) so the report's pass/fail column is grounded in the spec.\n3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` as the CLI binary. Argument surface: `--scope`, `--time-range`, `--signals`, `--baseline <path>`, `--benchmark <path>`, `--format text|json|ci-summary`, `--output <path>`, `--fail-on-regression`. The binary loads the current metrics via the T65 collector against the active workspace, optionally loads a baseline JSON, optionally loads the T66 benchmark JSON, and renders the `RegressionReport` to stdout or the `--output` path. With `--fail-on-regression`, exits non-zero when any signal fails its spec §Measurable Success Criteria target.\n4. Author `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` describing: report architecture, signal definitions (referencing T65), thresholds (referencing spec §Measurable Success Criteria), input/output formats, CI integration guidance, regression-investigation runbook. The doc is the operator-facing reference.\n5. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report_tests.rs` covering: (a) deterministic rendering across all three formats; (b) baseline-vs-current delta computation; (c) target threshold pass/fail logic for each spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target; (d) honest reporting of `null` signals (renders as `n/a` with reason, never as zero); (e) exit-code behavior of `--fail-on-regression`; (f) per-signal evidence-pointer round-trip.\n6. Wire the binary into the workspace `Cargo.toml` so `cargo build --release --bin lattice_report` produces an installable binary. Document the build/deploy path in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n7. Workspace boundary: the CLI honors the workspace it was invoked against — it never crosses workspace boundaries even if multiple `.lattice/` paths are reachable.\n8. Honor Cadres coding standard `## Observability`: the CLI emits structured `tracing` output to stderr so CI logs capture every signal collected and every threshold evaluated.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — `lattice_report` CLI binary collecting current metrics, optionally loading baseline + T66 benchmark JSON, rendering the regression report in text/json/ci-summary, exiting non-zero on regression when requested.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report.rs` — `RegressionReport`, `ReportInput`, `SuccessCriteriaThresholds`, three renderers, per-signal evidence pointers; encodes spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets explicitly.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report_tests.rs` — unit tests covering deterministic rendering, baseline delta, threshold pass/fail, honest null handling, exit-code behavior, evidence-pointer round-trip.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` — operator-facing reference: architecture, signal definitions, thresholds, formats, CI integration, regression runbook.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — confirms the binary entry point exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` — confirms the operator doc exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release --bin lattice_report` — the binary compiles cleanly with the rest of the workspace.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::report_tests` — every report test passes (rendering determinism, baseline delta, threshold logic, null handling, exit-code behavior, evidence-pointer round-trip).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split `report.rs` per renderer if needed).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `RegressionReport`, `ReportInput`, `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone`; JSON output schema documented in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n- No silent error handling — every IO/parse failure surfaces with a typed error and a non-zero exit code; honest `null` values render as `n/a` with reason, never zero.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`SuccessCriteriaThresholds::memory_inclusion_precision`, not `Thresholds::mip`).\n- For SQLite: storage access goes through T65 `MetricsCollector`; no raw SQL in the binary or report module.\n- Observability: binary emits structured `tracing` to stderr with `scope`, `signal_count`, `pass_count`, `fail_count`, `format` fields per invocation.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation` and `## Measurable Success Criteria` in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` and the binary source.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all three render formats ship; `--fail-on-regression` is implemented; the operator doc is complete (no \"TBD\" sections).\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; the existing `lattice` daemon binary is unaffected.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3269,"cache_read_input_tokens":103711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3269,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"279282f3-a4da-48f1-994d-a044bce886f7","request_id":"req_011Cb7NY8HNbB9Meugrxe9qx","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T41.log:1981:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2749:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:867:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MPB6E3V4a7oByv1GVt2tnV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013HQsYfpzN9F19m4z35f4hY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md","content":"# T69 — Phase 9 — Metrics regression coverage tests (success-criteria targets from spec)\n\n**Phase:** 9\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T65, T66, T67, T68\n**Spec anchor:** [§Measurable Success Criteria](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#measurable-success-criteria)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task ships the regression tests that prove the cognitive workspace fork beats the baselines on every initial target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria. The tests run the redesigned tools (T56/T57) against the T66 fixture repos, feed the captured events into the T65 metrics collector, render the T68 regression report, and assert each spec §Measurable Success Criteria target. Without this task, the metrics infrastructure exists but no automated gate proves the system meets its stated goals — the Phase 9 DoD (\"changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote\") would not be satisfied.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Initial targets: 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads; 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks; zero trusted display of known contradicted memory; zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks.\" (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)\n\n> \"Definition of done: changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n> \"The fork should beat current Lattice on: lower tool calls per coding task; lower irrelevant context inclusion; higher relevant file/symbol recall; higher memory reuse precision; lower stale memory surfacing; better repeated-failure avoidance; better test recommendation accuracy; better user correction retention; faster diagnosis from failures; more explainable context selection.\" (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T65 — `MetricsCollector`, `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`.\n  - T66 — fixture repos + `golden_anchors.json` + `cognitive_workspace_benchmark`.\n  - T67 — `metrics_surface` (per-call relevance is needed for `IrrelevantFilesOpenedPerTask` and inclusion-precision assertions).\n  - T68 — `RegressionReport`, `SuccessCriteriaThresholds`, `lattice_report` binary.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` (from T04) — baseline column for delta-based assertions (30% fewer, 40% fewer).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/` — module from T65.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/` and `memory_v2/` — tools under test.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Tests as documentation`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Measurable Success Criteria and §Phase 9 DoD in full. Quote the \"Initial targets\" paragraph verbatim into a module-level doc comment on `metrics/regression_tests.rs` so the thresholds are visible at the test source.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/regression_tests.rs` containing one `#[test]` per spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target. Each test loads the T66 fixtures, runs the redesigned tools end-to-end against the golden tasks, feeds events into the T65 `MetricsCollector`, and asserts the corresponding threshold using the T68 `SuccessCriteriaThresholds`:\n   - `test_discovery_tool_calls_at_least_30pct_below_baseline` — `ToolCallsPerSuccessfulTask` is ≥30% below the baseline value from `baseline_metrics.json` for the discovery-tool subset.\n   - `test_irrelevant_file_reads_at_least_40pct_below_baseline` — `IrrelevantFilesOpenedPerTask` is ≥40% below baseline.\n   - `test_memory_inclusion_precision_at_least_80pct` — `MemoryInclusionPrecision` ≥ 0.80 on the curated memory benchmark tasks from T66.\n   - `test_zero_trusted_display_of_contradicted_memory` — `ContradictionMissedRate` equals 0 across all fixture tasks.\n   - `test_zero_trusted_display_of_stale_memory_without_label` — `StaleMemorySurfacedRate` equals 0 across all fixture tasks (stale memories may appear, but never without an explicit stale label per spec §Phase 7 DoD).\n   - `test_relevant_test_recommendation_at_least_90pct` — `TestsRecommendedVsNeeded` recall ≥ 0.90 on the curated tasks from T66.\n3. Each test must surface a useful failure diagnostic: when an assertion fails, print the per-signal `MetricValue` plus the contributing event/memory evidence pointers from T68 so the regression is investigable without re-running.\n4. Mark long-running tests `#[ignore]` only if they exceed CI budget; the verification command runs with `-- --include-ignored` so CI executes them. Spec §Tests as documentation forbids silently skipping required coverage.\n5. Implement a helper `MetricsTestHarness` in the same file (or a sibling `regression_harness.rs`) that loads fixtures deterministically, executes a fixed tool sequence per task, captures events into an isolated `.lattice/events.db`, and returns the resulting `MetricValue`s. The harness encapsulates the deterministic-seed and fixture-freeze policy from T66 so per-test code is short.\n6. Add an explicit assertion at the top of the file that `baseline_metrics.json` exists; if not, the tests fail fast with a clear error pointing to T04 rather than passing accidentally.\n7. Workspace boundary + scope: every harness invocation runs in an isolated workspace under a temp directory; never reuses or contaminates the developer's local `.lattice/`.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/regression_tests.rs` — one `#[test]` per spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target asserting the redesigned system beats baselines (30% discovery, 40% irrelevant reads, 80% memory precision, 0 stale/contradicted trusted display, 90% test recommendation); shared `MetricsTestHarness` for deterministic fixture execution; per-failure diagnostics via T68 evidence pointers.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/regression_tests.rs` — confirms the regression-tests file exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::regression_tests -- --include-ignored` — every spec §Measurable Success Criteria regression test passes against the T66 fixture repos.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (split into `regression_tests.rs` + `regression_harness.rs` if needed).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: each test reads thresholds from the T68 `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` rather than hard-coding numbers in two places; signal names use the T65 `MetricSignal` enum.\n- No silent error handling — every fixture load / harness failure produces a typed error; no test uses `unwrap()` on a `Result` that could legitimately fail without diagnostic.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no `#[ignore]` without a written reason; no skipped assertions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`MetricsTestHarness::run_fixture_task`, not `MetricsTestHarness::go`).\n- For SQLite: temp DBs only; harness cleans up on completion.\n- Observability: each test emits `tracing::info!` with `signal`, `target`, `actual`, `pass` fields on completion.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Measurable Success Criteria` and `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation` in module doc comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every one of the six spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets has a corresponding `#[test]`; no target is punted with a placeholder.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3556,"cache_read_input_tokens":106980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3556,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"3f844d71-255e-43d5-a676-4efcaa90f907","request_id":"req_011Cb7NbRkgeaFKnUV3Q7p7E","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T41.log:1982:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2750:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:876:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LN1e4xG5mvzKzrETeuvqjR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vrek2dy1xWmMF51dSANLpm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R70.md","content":"# R70 — Tests/Docs review — Phase 9 metrics + evaluation\n\n**Phase:** 9\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T65, T66, T67, T68, T69\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`); Definition of Done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the Phase 9 review. It asserts that the metrics collection module (T65), the cross-language benchmark fixture repository (T66), the MCP-wired metrics surface (T67), the regression dashboard + CLI report (T68), and the regression coverage tests (T69) together satisfy spec §Phase 9 deliverables and definition of done, and that each spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target is either met by T69's tests or recorded as a `fail` finding triggering reopen. Without this review, Phase 10 (Human Review UI) proceeds against an unvalidated metrics layer and the success-criterion claims cannot be defended.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 9 Deliverables: retrieval relevance metrics; memory usefulness metrics; context token efficiency metrics; stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics; test-pass-after-plan metrics; repeated-failure reduction metrics; benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors; regression dashboard or CLI report.\"\n\n> \"Required metrics: tool calls per successful task; irrelevant files opened per task; relevant anchor recall; memory inclusion precision; memory later-used rate; stale memory surfaced rate; contradiction missed rate; tests recommended versus tests needed; workflow success after first plan.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n> \"Initial targets: 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads; 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks; zero trusted display of known contradicted memory; zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks.\" (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)\n\n> \"Definition of done: changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T65 — `metrics/{mod, signals, signals_tests}.rs`.\n  - T66 — `benches/fixtures/{README, rust-repo/manifest, typescript-repo/manifest, python-repo/manifest, golden_anchors.json}` + `cognitive_workspace_benchmark.rs`.\n  - T67 — `rpc/{metrics_surface, metrics_surface_tests}.rs`.\n  - T68 — `bin/lattice_report.rs`, `metrics/{report, report_tests}.rs`, `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n  - T69 — `metrics/regression_tests.rs`.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` (from T04) — baseline column referenced by T69.\n  - The reviews directory `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/`.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Tests as documentation`, `## Observability`; Definition of Done checklist.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 9 and §Measurable Success Criteria in full. Quote the \"Required metrics\" paragraph and the \"Initial targets\" paragraph verbatim at the top of the review.\n2. Under `## Spec alignment`, walk every Phase 9 deliverable (retrieval relevance metrics, memory usefulness metrics, context token efficiency metrics, stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics, test-pass-after-plan metrics, repeated-failure reduction metrics, benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors, regression dashboard/CLI report) and cite the implementing files from T65–T69. Flag any deliverable that is missing or partial.\n3. Under `## Coding-standard alignment`, run a per-file check across `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs`, and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/cognitive_workspace_benchmark.rs`: file length ≤800 lines, function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10, schema parity (every public type serde-derived), no `TODO`/`FIXME`/commented-out code, no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`, observability spans present, honest `None` reporting on missing data (no fabricated zeros). Record each violation with file:line.\n4. Under `## Success-criteria coverage`, build a matrix of every spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target (six rows: 30% discovery, 40% irrelevant reads, 80% memory precision, 0 stale-without-label, 0 contradicted-trusted, 90% test recommendation). For each row, cite the T69 `#[test]` name proving the target, the current measured value on the T66 fixtures, the baseline value from T04, and the pass/fail outcome. Any row without a passing test is a `fail` finding.\n5. Under `## Findings`, summarize spec gaps, coding-standard violations, threshold-coverage misses, fixture coverage gaps (e.g. one language fixture missing a task class), honest-null violations, and any divergence between the T68 CLI report output and the T65 collector. Each finding cites file:line and the spec or standard it violates.\n6. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::metrics_surface_tests` and `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench cognitive_workspace_benchmark -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3`. Record each result in the review.\n7. Under `## Verdict`, state `pass` or `fail` with a one-paragraph justification. If `fail`, name the specific tasks that must be reopened.\n8. Save the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` with the mandatory headings checked by verification commands.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — structured Phase 9 review with `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Success-criteria coverage`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict` headings; per-deliverable spec citations; per-file standard checks; per-target threshold matrix; build/test/bench results; verdict with reopen list if `fail`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms the review exists at the harness path.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms spec alignment is recorded under a dedicated heading.\n- `grep -q '## Success-criteria coverage' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms the threshold matrix is recorded under a dedicated heading rather than buried in prose.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms a verdict is stated under a dedicated heading.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — not applicable (review doc).\n- No `T